      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_cannot_be_controlled_by_adversary",
      "reason": "Missing macro expansion limit in the ImageMagick MVG decoder. ImageMagick 7.1.1-43 selects MVG only from an explicit mvg: prefix or a .mvg file name, because coders/mvg.h declares no magic signature. LaTeXML passes only resolved local graphic paths, submitted LaTeX project members are limited to .tex, .bib, .sty, .cls, .bst, .png, .jpg, .jpeg, .pdf, .eps, .svg and .txt names without colons, and LaTeXML keeps \\openout and filecontents output in memory, so submitted content cannot be decoded as MVG. The image's ImageMagick policy also denies the MVG coder, so even an explicit mvg: prefix is refused.",
      "reviewed": "2026-10-22",
      "expires": "2027-01-20",
      "disclosure": "docs/security/known-unfixed-advisories-0.9.12.md"
