      "reason": "Coder-domain policy bypass: ImageMagick 7.1.1-43 checks the requested format name, matched case-sensitively, instead of the name of the coder it resolves case-insensitively. The image's policy denies every coder with a * rule and then allows only the upper-case names PNG, JPEG, JPG, EPS, PDF and PAM, so a request whose name differs from the coder's only in case matches just the deny-all rule and is refused; it cannot reach a coder the policy does not allow. The native image check confirms that an Mvg: prefix is refused as MVG.",
