      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "vulnerable_code_not_present",
      "reason": "Integer-conversion error in the PSD resource-block parser (coders/psd.c ParseImageResourceBlocks) that causes an infinite loop on 32-bit builds only, as the upstream advisory and fix f053f778 state: the block length is read into a 32-bit unsigned int and cast to ssize_t, which only overflows where ssize_t is 32-bit. The API image is built for 64-bit targets (amd64 and arm64), where ssize_t is 64-bit and the bounds check holds, so the vulnerable path is not present. Independently, the image's ImageMagick policy denies the PSD coder, confirmed in the image and through the LaTeXML launcher by explicit prefix, by extension and by content sniffing of a .png-named file, so PSD is never decoded regardless of word size.",
      "reviewed": "2026-10-22",
      "expires": "2027-01-20",
      "disclosure": "docs/security/known-unfixed-advisories-0.9.12.md"
